I've been a long-time fan of Ark. I had racked in about 2k ish of my time spent playing on official servers. The moment the flyer nerf came I left official altogether. I always had hope that regardless of the; ♥♥♥♥♥♥ optimization, the pathetic excuse of patch updates, the evidently care-free take the devs have, even the obviously ♥♥♥♥♥♥ dino models, and the mega-alpha tribes that take over literally every and any server available to pvp users, that in spite of all of that which is wrong with the game, I had thought the devs were going to stick with us PLAYERS the ones who have been here since before the official release. Oh, how wrong I was.
Graphics: Absolutely stunning. The first thing that really hooked me into the game at all was the graphics. It looks so damn good, it's unbelievable just how good such a small company (at the time) could make such a beautiful game;
Modding: There is a Devkit available that allows modders to basically make an entirely new game. I've used my fair share of mods and I'll tell you that using mods was the best damn decision i've ever made relating to this game. The modding community is well and thriving, although most modders don't get compensation in the manner in which they deserver they still do it out of the kindness of their heart. I love that so much about this community;
Sound: The sounds of the game are incredible and are just getting better with each update to it. The orchestral soundtracks are awe-inspiring. I never really took notice of the soundtrack at first but with each playthrough I feel more and more immersed into my gameplay as I hear the soundtrack for a dino in pursuit of me, my adreniline starts pumping as i squeel like an adolescent girl whilst running from a Rex or worst of all a Giga;
Gameplay: The taming definitely kept me on my toes, it didn't matter how far i'd gotten in-game the taming is and always will be the most entertaining aspect of this game. I always have to be aware of everything around me and my tame, if not a wild compy or worse a wild rex could come along and ruin my taming efficiency altogether.
Gameplay: As is rather clear I don't have much good to say about the mechanics of the game if any, why is that? Well for starters the game is flawed at it's most basic level, the building mechanics of the vanilla game are so goddamn awful that modders actually had to fix it themselves to get any degree of satisfaction out of building. There's a number of clipping issues, not to mention the array of problems with tek tier being introduced. I've always been interested in build and survive type of games. However Ark's building mechanics are so buggy to the point in which having to deal with bugs on a day to day basis could very well drive you insane. It seems that the devs are fully aware of the♥♥♥♥♥♥stain that is their building mechanics as they have publically sponsored "Structures Plus" which is a mod aimed to improve the players' ability to create whatever architectural masterpiece they wish to. Don't get me started on PvP... The reason most players stray from PvP in Ark the moment they decide to join that mess of servers they're greeted with the rudest wake up call. There are no "official pvp" servers there are only servers that weren't attained by Mega-Alpha tribes and servers that they have yet to take. The reality is that the devs are stupid enough to decide that what the PvP users want is what the PvE users need. If there is enough wimps in pvp that whine about a dino being op, they'll nerf it to the ground, realize their mistake and take months if not a solid year to fix it. Now to get to the worst culprit of what's ruinning this game. THE ♥♥♥♥ING GRIND. Look I recognize that a lot of players are okay with the grind, and in fact enjoy it because they feel it makes the end-game feel much more rewarding. You know what I say to them? ♥♥♥♥ YOU. Adding more grind to the base-game DOES NOT AND WILL NEVER add to the gameplay experience, if anything it strips it from casual players. Suppose you are an individual with this thing called a "life" and don't have 100 hours to raise a baby dino, or truly fortify and upgrade your house and tame the dinos necessary to have proper protection from other players or dinos. What then? Nothing. You can literally do nothing but sacrifice the time you would have spent having a life or waste your time grinding rather than; doing your homework, going to work, walking your dog, doing your chores, literally anything irl. It doesn't feel rewarding, it mostly just feels like you're life is slowly being stripped away piece by piece as you further progress towards the end-game.
Dinos: I ABSOLUTELY HATE that the devs didn't even freaking bother to correctly scale the dino models to what they're real size is. I get it, it's a game what should I care... The problem is that a lot of people care, even those who are still playing to this day. I've never liked how ♥♥♥♥♥♥ the dino models are, yeah they're pretty but at least hire a paleontologist to get some degree of info and make the dino models accordingly not any of this nonsense scaling they have in-game. It's just disappointing seeing a game with so much potential fail so miserably. I'll never understand why the devs feel so compelled to ruin everyone's experience rather than just the pve official server users. If the majority of pvp users want to whine about something enough for the devs to make a change, congrats you guys accomplished something with your yelling. Fine, whatever. Just DON'T PUSH THE CHANGES TO PVE. I'll never understand why they can't get this through their thick skulls. The flyer nerf created an onslaught of negative reviews because of the devs "The change is permanent and we clearly don't give a ♥♥♥♥ about our player-base" attitude. Needless to say the dino AI is rather clunky, the dinos just seem to wonder with no clear objective. I understand it must be either impossible or extremely difficult to make them do otherwise, but could the devs just polish that even a little?
All in all Ark is a decent game, it's certainly not worth the 60 dollar pricetag if anything it's 30 bucks maybe 35. The devs clearly have a carefree demeanor about them when it comes to what actually has to be done to further improve the game  and increase the pleasure a user will get out of their gaming experience. It's hard hitting to know that the devs aren't ever going to listen to the majority of users only the few that whine and scream the loudest. Hell even when the majority mimicks the few (ie. what most players did with the flyer nerf) they still don't care, they're the type to simply give a vague response and will NEVER really answer the question head on. It pisses me off going through some of the devs responses, they're either flat out rude, or they downright avoid a quesion but reply simply to prove that they ARE listening but just don't care. The dino models could be easily re-done what with their influx of cash with the full release of the game and the dlc that will follow. The game has many many MANY flaws but as always with a game with so much potentional the modding community is always on top of that♥♥♥♥♥♥either by providing solutions to the devs themselves or simply creating a mod to deal with certain things the player base has always wanted or needed. Don't get me wrong, I enjoyed some of the hours I put into this game, even on official servers with the absolutely absurd amount of grind. It felt great finally being able to tame a giga, and raising my first quetz. I've wasted my life enjoying this hollow "masterpiece".

